f the mucous membranes, leading to significant complications such as dysphagia and difficulties with nutritional intake. It is reported that mucositis has a high incidence rate, occurring in approximately 70% of patients undergoing intensive chemotherapy treatments. \n\nThe condition can severely impact a patient's ability to eat, making nutritional intervention necessary. Mucositis is especially prevalent among patients receiving high-dose chemotherapy and those undergoing radiotherapy, including those who have undergone hematopoietic cell transplants. \n\nManagement strategies for mucositis may include the administration of oral glutamine, which has been shown to reduce the duration and severity of the condition. Overall, mucositis is a painful and challenging side effect of cancer treatments that requires careful attention to ensure adequate nutrition and patient comfort.", "ENFERMEDAD INJERTO CONTRA HUÉSPED:Graft-versus-host disease (EICH), also known as \"ENFERMEDAD INJERTO CONTRA HUÉSPED,\" is a condition that arises in allogeneic transplants, where donor cells attack the recipient's body. This disease primarily affects the skin, liver, and intestines, with an incidence rate ranging from 30% to 40%. It is a significant complication following hematopoietic stem cell transplantation (TPH), highlighting the challenges associated with immune responses in transplant medicine.", "ENFERMEDAD VENOOCLOSIVA HEPÁTICA:Hepatic veno-occlusive disease (EVOH), a complication that can occur after hematopoietic stem cell transplantation, affecting the liver.", "ENFERMEDAD VENOCLOSIVA HEPÁTICA:Complicación que puede aparecer en trasplantes autólogos y alogénicos, con una incidencia del 20% de los pacientes, que puede llevar a fallo múltiple.", "NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL HIPERPROTEICA:Intervención nutricional que puede ser necesaria en caso de desnutrición previa al trasplante.", "NPT:NPT, which stands for Nutrición Parenteral Total or Nutritional Parenteral Therapy, is a method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who are unable to eat or absorb nutrients through their gastrointestinal tract. This nutritional support is particularly crucial for patients during their hospital stay and is also utilized for infants who cannot receive adequate nutrition through oral feeding. NPT is specifically indicated for individuals with conditions such as severe pancreatitis, where oral intake is not possible or tolerated. Overall, NPT serves as a vital intervention for those requiring nutritional support when traditional feeding methods are not feasible.", "TRASPLANTE AUTÓLOGO:Tipo de trasplante donde las células provienen del propio paciente, sin riesgo de EICH.", "TRASPLANTE ALOGÉNICO:Tipo de trasplante donde las células provienen de un donante, con riesgo de EICH.", "APLASIA MEDULAR:Condición que se presenta en el postrasplante inmediato, relacionada con la reducción de células sanguíneas.", "INFECCIONES:The entity \"INFECCIONES\" encompasses a range of complications that can significantly impact patient health across various medical contexts. Infections are particularly prevalent in patients undergoing different phases of transplantation, especially those who have received hematopoietic cell transplants, due to the immunosuppression associated with these procedures. Additionally, infections are a common concern in critically ill patients, where they can lead to increased morbidity and mortality.\n\nPatients with specific conditions, such as neutropenia—especially in cases of type Ib glycogen storage disease—are at a heightened risk for infections. The elderly population, particularly those who are malnourished, also face significant health risks from infections. Furthermore, infections can complicate the health of patients with chronic liver diseases and are frequently associated with catheter use, leading to serious health issues.\n\nIn surgical patients, infections are a common complication that can hinder recovery and are often evaluated in studies related to nutritional support. Infections can also contribute to the formation of intestinal fistulas, complicating treatment and recovery processes. Moreover, nutritional requirements may be altered in patients with conditions like cerebrovascular disease, which can further influence their susceptibility to infections. \n\nOverall, infections represent a critical health challenge across various patient populations, necessitating careful management and preventive strategies to mitigate their impact on health outcomes.", "REACCIONES ADVERSAS MEDICAMENTOSAS:Efectos secundarios que pueden ocurrir en pacientes postrasplante debido a la medicación.", "ALTERACIONES METABÓLICAS:ALTERACIONES METABÓLICAS se refiere a cambios en el metabolismo que pueden ocurrir en pacientes trasplantados, así como en aquellos con enfermedad hepática crónica. Estas alteraciones pueden afectar la salud general de los pacientes, impactando específicamente en el manejo de la glucosa, proteínas y lípidos en el organismo.", "EICH CRÓNICA:EICH CRÓNICA, o enfermedad injerto contra huésped crónica, es una forma prolongada de la enfermedad que puede manifestarse en el postrasplante tardío. Esta condición aparece generalmente después del día 100 del trasplante y se caracteriza por la aparición de infecciones recurrentes y afectaciones en múltiples órganos. Debido a su naturaleza prolongada, la EICH crónica requiere un manejo médico continuo y cuidadoso para abordar sus complicaciones y mejorar la calidad de vida del paciente.", "TRASPLANTE:The term \"TRASPLANTE\" refers to various medical procedures involving the transfer of cells or organs to treat serious health conditions. One specific type is the hematopoietic cell transplant, which involves the transfer of stem cells to address diseases such as leukemia and other hematological disorders. Additionally, transplant procedures can lead to complications that necessitate specialized nutritional support for patients. Furthermore, transplantation may also be required for individuals suffering from severe liver damage, such as that caused by Wilson's disease. Overall, \"TRASPLANTE\" encompasses a range of surgical interventions aimed at improving health outcomes for patients with critical medical conditions.", "CICLOFOSFAMIDA:Ciclofosfamida is a medication that serves multiple purposes in medical treatment. It is primarily recognized as an immunosuppressive drug, which is utilized in clinical trials to address inflammatory responses in brain lesions of patients with Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). Additionally, ciclofosfamida is commonly used in oncological treatments. However, it is important for patients to take this medication with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. It is also noteworthy that ciclofosfamida can lead to malabsorption and malnutrition in patients, highlighting the need for careful monitoring during its use."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}